# VA-API driver with Apple Video Decoder fixes, maintained at omacom/libva-v4l2_request.
# The asahi and aurora aliases let libva discover it on Apple Silicon.
#
# J604 local build: the official recipe plus the patches listed below.
# pkgrel 2.622: rebased on the official pkgrel 2, which ships the aurora alias
# itself, so the local aurora alias of .604 is dropped. No source change.
#
# pkgrel .605: + H.264/HEVC encoding (VAEntrypointEncSlice) on V4L2 stateful encoders
# (the Apple video encoder), so VA-API screen recorders and browsers encode in hardware.
#
# pkgrel .608: + up to 16 bitstream buffers in flight (the AVD queues 16 frames in firmware).
# pkgrel .607: + VP9 takes its maximum frame size from the kernel (8192 on kernels that decode 8K VP9).
# pkgrel .606: + surfaces exported before their first decode are sized for 10-bit AV1 and
# VP9 too, so AV1 10-bit above 4096 pixels decodes on the AVD instead of being refused.
# pkgrel .616: + the encoder refuses a coded-buffer size its unsigned field cannot hold, keeps
# its input surface alive until the picture ends, and refuses another context's coded buffer.
# pkgrel .619: + a surface handed back while its CAPTURE buffer is busy is decoded into an idle
# spare buffer (up to 4) instead of waiting, also under FFmpeg's vaDeriveImage probe and its downloads.
# pkgrel .620: + when all 4 spares are busy, wait for the spare that frees first instead of the
# surface's own buffer, so the decoder queue does not drain (V4L2R_REBIND_FIRST=0 restores .619).
# pkgrel .621: + never rebind a surface while a derived image (vaDeriveImage) maps its buffer (PR 117 d4121bd).
# pkgrel 2.623: + a busy exported buffer is rebound too when the client exports the surface again after
# every decode (FFmpeg hwmap, mpv dma-buf interop), so playback keeps the decoder queue full
# (V4L2R_REBIND_EXPORTED=0 restores 2.622).
# pkgrel 2.624: + waiting for a decoded frame (vaSyncSurface) no longer holds the context lock, so a
# client syncing one frame does not stop the next from being queued (V4L2R_SYNC_UNLOCKED=0 restores 2.623).
# pkgrel 2.625: + that wait also releases the driver-wide API lock that vaBeginPicture takes, so the next frame
# really is queued while a frame is mapped (V4L2R_SYNC_UNLOCKED=0 restores 2.623).
# pkgrel 2.628: + offer packed H.264 sequence headers where the encoder takes the client's SPS words, so
# FFmpeg writes avcC and h264_vaapi encodes into Matroska; HEVC as 2.623 (no packed HEVC headers).
# pkgrel 2.629: + AV1 frames go to the AVD at EndPicture (no one-frame hold; V4L2R_AV1_HOLD=1 restores it).
# pkgrel 2.635: + the encoder keeps one OUTPUT index per input dma-buf (row 37 TERM2).
# pkgrel 2.636: + two pictures in flight and vaSyncBuffer, so FFmpeg encodes async (row 37 TERM1).
# pkgrel 2.637: + HEVC Main10 encoding from P010 surfaces where the encoder takes P010 (row 37 M10).

